    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/019DF7F6E271614BAB2785B88C6A379F/jobs/233474": {
      "title": "Assistant to the President and Vice Presidents",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant to the President and Vice Presidents Hot Job Wilmington, DE 19808 Start Date 10/01/2026 Apply Overview Salary Range $68,000.00 - $70,000.00 Salary/year Apply Assistant to the President and Vice Presidents Position Summary The holder of this position provides confidential administrative and clerical support to the President and the Vice Presidents of the College. The position serves as a central coordinator for executive scheduling, correspondence, meetings, travel, reports, and office operations while providing exceptional customer service to internal and external constituents. The holder of the position works closely with senior leaders to ensure efficient administrative operations, effective communication, and seamless coordination of executive activities across the College. Key Responsibilities Assist the President and Vice Presidents in the discharge of day-to-day responsibilities, including assisting with the coordination of projects across the President and Vice President areas. Coordinate communications, meeting logistics and materials for the President, the Executive Leadership Team, and the Board of Trustees. Prepare correspondence, reports, presentations, meeting materials, and meeting minutes. Assist the President with public relations within the College Community and the outside community. Lead planning and coordination for the annual holiday luncheon and the Employee Recognition and Retirement luncheon, in partnership with Human Resources and other campus stakeholders. Assist with commencement, convocation, Homecoming, presidential events and special projects. Assist with budget preparation and oversight for the President’s Office. Monitor budget expenditures, assuring expense documentation is in place and expenses are charged to appropriate categories. Qualifications Associate’s degree required; Bachelor’s Degree preferred with at least five (5) years’ executive administrative support experience. Reports To: President Months per Year: 12 months Hours per Week: 37.5 FLSA: Non-Exempt Position Category: NE8 Salary Range: $68,000 - $70,000 Benefits: Goldey-Beacom College offers an excellent benefits package that includes: Medical, Dental, & Vision Retirement Plan (403b) in which College contributes 5.5% Life & Disability Insurances Education benefits for employees, spouses and dependents Generous PTO (This position starts at 17 days of personal time-off for the calendar year Prorated based on start date) Paid Holidays, paid two-week winter break and ½ day Fridays during the summer Free weekly meals in dining hall. Free parking Application Instructions Interested applicants must fully complete and sign the employment application. Applicants should submit a cover letter, resume/CV and contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. About Goldey‑Beacom College Goldey‑Beacom College, located in Wilmington, Delaware, is a private institution with a proud history of academic excellence, personal attention, and student‑centered service. The College is committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive environment where students are encouraged to achieve their highest potential and where employees are expected to uphold the highest standards of professionalism, integrity, and respect. Goldey-Beacom College recognizes the importance of being an equal opportunity employer that fosters an inclusive, equitable and respectful campus climate. We are constantly working to create a College that celebrates individuality and strives to provide a non-discriminatory, fair and equitable learning and working environment for the GBC family. While we celebrate diversity in all forms, our hiring, compensation, training, and employment decisions are based on merit, qualifications, and performance. We are governed by transparency and accountability in our human resource policies and procedures, recruitment and selection, hiring, training and development, employee relations, promotion, compensation and total rewards, and termination. Please feel free to share this job posting with others or other job sites to assist the College in expanding the pool of candidates. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/019DF7F6E271614BAB2785B88C6A379F/jobs/232922": {
      "title": "Practicum Coordinator",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Practicum Coordinator Hot Job Wilmington, DE 19808 Start Date 09/25/2026 Apply Overview Salary Range $28.00 - $30.00 Hourly Position Type Part Time Education Level Graduate Degree Apply Interim Practicum Coordinator Position Summary Goldey-Beacom College invites applications for an in-person Interim Practicum Coordinator to support the Master of Arts in Counseling Program until June 30, 2027, or until a full-time coordinator has been secured. This interim role is designed to provide focused coordination, continuity, and process support for student practicum experiences. The successful candidate will be highly organized, student-centered, and familiar with clinical training expectations in counselor education or a related field. The Interim Practicum Coordinator will review current practicum sites, support students preparing for placement, monitor documentation for students currently in practicum, reaffirm relationships with site supervisors, and help strengthen the overall practicum process in alignment with program expectations, institutional policies, and applicable accreditation standards. Key Responsibilities • Review existing practicum sites to ensure continued appropriateness, quality, and alignment with program and accreditation expectations. • Review students eligible for practicum to determine progress toward placement readiness and identify outstanding requirements or barriers. • Monitor students currently engaged in practicum placements to ensure required paperwork, approvals, evaluations, and related documentation remain current and complete. • Communicate with students regarding practicum timelines, expectations, documentation requirements, and placement-related next steps. • Reaffirm and strengthen relationships with practicum site supervisors and community partners. • Serve as a liaison among students, site supervisors, program faculty, and relevant administrative offices to support successful practicum experiences. • Assist in identifying gaps, risks, or inefficiencies in the practicum process and recommend practical improvements. • Support compliance with institutional policies and applicable accreditation standards related to supervised clinical training experiences. • Maintain accurate records and provide updates to program leadership regarding practicum site status, student placement progress, and documentation completion. Qualifications • Master’s degree in Counselor Education, Counseling, Psychology, Higher Education, Student Affairs, or a closely related field required. • Experience with clinical training coordination, field placement, practicum/internship administration, academic advising, or related student support functions. • Familiarity with counselor education practicum/internship processes and CACREP standards preferred. • Strong organizational, recordkeeping, communication, and relationship-management skills. • Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, site supervisors, and external partners. • Demonstrated commitment to student success, professional preparation, and high-quality experiential learning. • Ability to manage multiple priorities, follow through on details, and support process improvement during an interim appointment. • Licensed professional preferred. Reports To: Provost/Vice President for Academic Affairs Months per Year: 12 months Hours per Week: 28 FLSA: Non-Exempt Position Category: NE7 Salary Range: $28 - $30 Hourly Benefits: Goldey-Beacom College offers an excellent benefits package that includes: Retirement Plan (403b) in which College contributes 5.5% Education benefits for employees, spouses and dependents Paid Holidays Free weekly meals in dining hall Free parking Application Instructions Interested applicants must fully complete and sign the employment application. Applicants should submit a cover letter, resume/CV and contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. About Goldey‑Beacom College Goldey‑Beacom College, located in Wilmington, Delaware, is a private institution with a proud history of academic excellence, personal attention, and student‑centered service. The College is committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive environment where students are encouraged to achieve their highest potential and where employees are expected to uphold the highest standards of professionalism, integrity, and respect. Goldey-Beacom College recognizes the importance of being an equal opportunity employer that fosters an inclusive, equitable and respectful campus climate. We are constantly working to create a College that celebrates individuality and strives to provide a non-discriminatory, fair and equitable learning and working environment for the GBC family. While we celebrate diversity in all forms, our hiring, compensation, training, and employment decisions are based on merit, qualifications, and performance. We are governed by transparency and accountability in our human resource policies and procedures, recruitment and selection, hiring, training and development, employee relations, promotion, compensation and total rewards, and termination. Please feel free to share this job posting with others or other job sites to assist the College in expanding the pool of candidates. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
