    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/019DF7F6E271614BAB2785B88C6A379F/jobs/224436": {
      "title": "Dean of Enrollment and Marketing",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Dean of Enrollment and Marketing Hot Job Wilmington, DE 19808 Start Date 08/10/2026 Apply Overview Salary Range $135,000.00 - $155,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Education Level Graduate Degree Apply Description Goldey‑Beacom College invites applications for the position of Dean of Enrollment and Marketing, a senior administrative role that serves as the College’s chief strategist and senior leader for recruitment, student financial aid, and marketing. The position provides vision, leadership and accountability for achieving the College’s enrollment, net tuition revenue, and market positioning. The Dean develops and directs strategies to support the College’s long-term sustainability and growth. The Dean supervises the Directors of Admissions, Marketing and Financial Aid, ensuring alignment of departmental priorities and institutional goals established by the President and the Executive Leadership Team. Primary Responsibilities Serve as the College's senior enrollment officer and principal advisor to the President regarding enrollment strategy, market position, prospective student demand, pricing strategy, and demographic trends. Develop and recommend recruitment and revenue objectives that support the College's strategic plan and financial sustainability. Lead the integration of admissions, financial aid, and marketing, into a unified strategic framework that meets annual recruitment and net revenue goals. Identify emerging risks and opportunities affecting enrollment and recommend strategic responses. Lead transformational initiatives designed to enhance recruitment effectiveness and market competitiveness. Provide strategic leadership toward measurable outcomes for Admissions, Marketing and Student Financial Aid. Serve as a member of the Executive Leadership Team and assist the President in strategic planning, decision making, crisis management, and communication. Develop and execute a comprehensive, innovative, data-informed enrollment strategy for undergraduate, adult learning and graduate programs for both domestic and international students. Advance sustainable enrollment growth while meeting net tuition revenue and student headcount goals. Utilize market research and predictive analytics to inform recruitment strategies and territory management. Utilize analytics and data to inform recruitment strategies, optimize marketing campaigns and assess financial aid effectiveness. Collaborate with key stakeholders in developing and proactively adjusting recruitment plans and strategies based on data analysis, review of application and enrollment trends and other metrics to effectively reach student enrollment and retention goals. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree with at least eight years of experience in a related field. At least five years of progressively responsible experience in admissions, enrollment management, student financial services or a related field in higher education. Supervisory experience overseeing multiple staff and departments. Knowledge of services, as well as state and federal regulations supporting a comprehensive recruitment, admissions and financial aid program. Strong analytical, communication, and interpersonal skills. Commitment to the College’s philosophy of customer service, continuous improvement, and community engagement. Reports To: The President Months per Year: 12 months FLSA: Exempt Position Category: E8 Salary Range: $135,000 - $155,000 Benefits: Goldey-Beacom College offers an excellent benefits package that includes: Medical, Dental, & Vision Retirement Plan (403b) in which College contributes 7.5% for this position level Life & Disability Insurances Education benefits for employees, spouses and dependents Generous PTO (27 days for this position level. Prorated for the first year) Paid Holidays, Paid two-week winter break and ½ day Fridays during the summer Free weekly meals in dining hall Free parking About Goldey‑Beacom College Goldey‑Beacom College, located in Wilmington, Delaware, is a private institution with a proud history of academic excellence, personal attention, and student‑centered service. The College is committed to fostering a welcoming and inclusive environment where students are encouraged to achieve their highest potential and where employees are expected to uphold the highest standards of professionalism, integrity, and respect. Goldey‑Beacom College invites applications for the position of Dean of Enrollment and Marketing, a senior administrative role that serves as the College’s chief strategist and senior leader for recruitment, student financial aid, and marketing. The position provides vision, leadership and accountability for achieving the College’s enrollment, net tuition revenue, and market positioning. The Dean develops and directs strategies to support the College’s long-term sustainability and growth. The Dean supervises the Directors of Admissions, Marketing and Financial Aid, ensuring alignment of departmental priorities and institutional goals established by the President and the Executive Leadership Team. Goldey-Beacom College recognizes the importance of being an equal opportunity employer that fosters an inclusive, equitable and respectful campus climate. We are constantly working to create a College that celebrates individuality and strives to provide a non-discriminatory, fair and equitable learning and working environment for the GBC family. While we celebrate diversity in all forms, our hiring, compensation, training, and employment decisions are based on merit, qualifications, and performance. We are governed by transparency and accountability in our human resource policies and procedures, recruitment and selection, hiring, training and development, employee relations, promotion, compensation and total rewards, and termination. Please feel free to share this job posting with others or other job sites to assist the College in expanding the pool of candidates. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
